<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: the partial sums a GNU ld A32 PLT stub builds its
    slot's address from are not filed as data references in the
    cross-reference index; the slot is.

    Issue:      kuna-analysis-armpltslot - `kuna xrefs` to an address inside
                a table placed between the PLT and the GOT answered the PLT
                stubs (`add ip,ip,#N,20` adds that address as an immediate),
                and every stub filed its PC value; the slot it jumps through
                was filed by none.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the on-demand cross-reference query
                (`listing/xrefs.rs`).

    The Listing tier and the xref query are built only on the real-object
    bootstrap path, never on the console decompile path (docs/spec/
    01-program-prep.md section 1.6), and no console command prints an xref
    row, so a stage test cannot assert the row itself. This case pins that
    the rule is inert in the rendered C of `main`, which calls `puts`,
    `printf` and `strlen` through the PLT stubs it concerns. The row-level
    proof (the slot as a Read and no partial sum) lives in the cargo gate
    `decompiler/crates/kuna-console/tests/verify_xreffp.rs`, over the
    `xreffp_arm_le32` fixture this case also loads.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; the pass clears it
    and loads the real linked ARM fixture (built from
    decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/xreffp_arm_le32.c).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/xreffp_arm_le32</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function main</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMPLTSLOT #1: main's call through the puts stub renders" min="1" max="1">^  puts\("hello"\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-ARMPLTSLOT #2: main's calls through the printf and strlen stubs render" min="1" max="1">^  printf\("%d %zu\\n",v1,strlen\(v2\)\);$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
